      "excerpt_sha256": "96a595eba27c49d99f6c9666d987119faba5b4ce94bcddc7f0a84f4cb3828b41",
      "excerpt_text": "NIH ODS explains that vitamin C supplements come in multiple forms (e.g., ascorbic acid, sodium/calcium ascorbate, and combination products such as Ester\u2011C). It reports that some human studies found similar plasma vitamin C across forms, and that authors concluded simple ascorbic acid is often the preferred source due to cost.",
