      "excerpt_sha256": "afc84b673bfda0013f75baea390e2b1a743e68b23b6bec6b63b34ab1d846ec11",
      "excerpt_text": "NIH ODS notes potassium in supplements is often potassium chloride, but other forms such as potassium citrate, phosphate, aspartate, bicarbonate, and gluconate are also used. It states Supplement Facts typically list elemental potassium rather than the salt weight.",
      "source": "NIH ODS",
      "url": "https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Potassium-HealthProfessional/"
    },
