      "excerpt_text": "NIH ODS notes that zinc bioavailability from vegetarian diets is often lower than from nonvegetarian diets because phytates in legumes and whole grains bind zinc and inhibit absorption. It also states that food preparation techniques that reduce phytate binding (e.g., soaking) and organic acids in fermented foods might increase zinc absorption.",
